+# MCP Server Checkup Report (`notes-mcp` on port 52749)
+
+**Overall Verdict:** **`has the problem`** (4 of the 10 checks fail — **C2, C5, C6, C10** — and the server also has the exact `resources/list` 401-after-`initialize` bug described in the colleague's preamble, plus several additional protocol/validation pitfalls).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Which Parts of the Colleague's Note Applied (and Which Did Not)
+
+### Parts That Applied
+1. **"Check if this applies to you" & Read-Only Ground Rules:**
+   - `notes-mcp` (`server.py`) is a remote Streamable HTTP MCP server listening at `http://127.0.0.1:52749/mcp`.
+   - All live checks were run strictly read-only: sending only `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, `server/discover`, `tools/list`, `resources/list`, `resources/templates/list`, `prompts/list`, and `tools/call` on tools marked `annotations.readOnlyHint: true` (`search_notes` and `get_note`). The write tool (`add_note`) was never called, no server files were modified, and the bearer token was read only from `$NOTES_TOKEN` without ever printing it.
+2. **Checks C1–C10:**
+   - **C1 (Anonymous `initialize`, `tools/list`, and `server/discover`), C2 (Refusals as `isError: true` vs. JSON-RPC error), C3 (Session survival after error), C4 (`outputSchema` validation on valid calls), C5 (Serialisation & `content` vs. `structuredContent` agreement), C7 (Per-call structured logging), C8 (Tool count and `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$` naming), C9 (Honest `"protocolVersion": "banana"` negotiation), and C10 (`outputSchema` corruption rejection)** all applied directly to the live server and local source code.
+   - **C6 (Surface lock & version drift)** applied in its local-source mode: computing the canonical surface fingerprint and checking the repository for a committed surface lock and test.
+3. **The Preamble Anecdote (`initialize` advertises `resources`, then `resources/list` returns `401`):**
+   - In paragraph 4 of the note, the colleague noted: *"the server advertises resources at `initialize` and then answers `resources/list` with a 401."*
+   - `server.py` has this **exact bug** (`server.py:138, 148-150`): `initialize` advertises `"resources": {"subscribe": false, "listChanged": false}` to anonymous callers, and then `resources/list`, `resources/read`, and `resources/templates/list` reject anonymous callers with HTTP `401 {"error": "unauthorized"}` — even though the only resource (`notes://guide`) is a static public usage guide.
+
+### Parts That Did Not Apply (Ignored)
+1. **Official MCP Registry lookup & `verify.mjs` (in C6):** `README.md` states *"Not yet listed in any registry"*, and external network queries are out of scope. Only the local fingerprint and surface-lock parts of C6 apply.
+2. **"Incomplete — record nothing" rule for auth-gated read tools:** Here, `initialize`, `tools/list`, and both read-only tools (`search_notes`, `get_note`) are open without a token, so C2–C5 ran in full.
+3. **Database `Decimal` encoder leakage example (in C5):** `server.py` loads static JSON from `notes.json` rather than a database returning `Decimal`. However, C5's rule that *"`content` text and `structuredContent` agree"* did apply and caught a bug in `search_notes`.
+4. **Recording `has_problem` / `no_problem` to worklore:** External reporting is prohibited by the ground rules.
+
